description:
FILED s534a (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) from the method-lookup evaluation (docs/method-lookup-eval-s534.md).  PRE-EXISTING on main 95a1de03 (code sha).

REPRODUCER (scratch/s534a/pr/ovl-order.pl in the s534a worktree):

    package A1; use overload 'bool' => sub { 0 }, '""' => sub { "A1" }, fallback => 1;
    package B1; our @ISA = ('A1');
    package B2; use overload 'bool' => sub { 1 }, '""' => sub { "B2" }, fallback => 1;
    package C;  our @ISA = ('B1', 'B2');
    package main;
    my $o = bless {}, 'C';
    print "bool=", ($o ? 1 : 0), " str=$o\n";

perl 5.40.3: `bool=0 str=A1` (C's MRO is C B1 A1 B2: A1's handlers are found first).  PCL: `bool=1 str=B2`.

MECHANISM: `%p-find-overload-mro` (cl/pcl-runtime.lisp, the overload section) is a two-pass walk: pass 1 looks in EVERY direct parent's table, pass 2 recurses into each parent.  So a grandparent on the FIRST parent's chain loses to a direct second parent.  perl's overload lookup is `gv_fetchmeth` of the `(OP` method -- the ordinary method resolution order, so the overload half and the method half must walk the SAME order (and under `use mro 'c3'` the C3 order -- #3631's half).  `%p-overload-fallback-of` and `%p-class-overloaded-p` walk depth-first already; only the handler walk is breadth-first.

FIX SHAPE: make the handler walk depth-first (the class, then each parent's whole chain in order), the order `p-method-call`'s @ISA walk uses -- ONE walk order for methods and overloads.  If #582's inherited cache (the s534a recommendation) lands first, its overload half mirrors whatever order the walk has, so this fix changes the recorder in the same place.  BAR: the reproducer prints perl's line; a guard row (two parents, both chains overload) in an existing overload Pl/t file; the companion op/overload legs one-file before/after (lib/overload.t).
